    "findings": [
      "The five trait tiers and wrappers agree across the final pages, config and map: four weapon families use 70/80/90/100%, Galvanic Rifle uses 30/40/50/60%; each tier value replaces the wrapper conditional .5 fallback. The generic consumer requires critical AND weakspot and adds one shared finesse-extra component, not whole-hit damage.",
      "All displayed arithmetic is correct under the stated assumptions: B=100,F=50,c=0,h=1 gives 150→200, +50 and 33.33%; B=100,F=100,c=.25,h=1 gives 225→325, +100 and 44.44%; Galvanic h=.6 gives 150→180, +30 and 20%.",
      "The map has exactly five variants and twelve bindings under kind ranged. Its weapon IDs, trait IDs, marks, tier values, exact UI-derived names, config and five reverse README rows agree. UI names are reconstructed from family/pattern/mark loc IDs and metadata/import/ukeys/append evidence; legacy display_name is not used.",
      "The final coverage distinguishes direct shots from weapon-specific actions: Autogun bash variants and Bolt Pistol melee and Galvanic bash can use the shared consumer when both hit flags qualify; Lasgun and Heavy Stubber special actions are flashlight toggles; the Galvanic beam is visual-only. Bolt Pistol secondary armor and hitmass-consumed explosions dispatch with is_critical_strike=false, including the kill/stop branch, and cannot receive this bonus.",
      "The held-slot wrapper is passive: no first-hit activation, stack, proc timer or fixed duration is claimed; switching away disables the held condition and switching back restores it, without claiming same-frame timing.",
      "RAW trait keys and English/zh-TW text share the recorded resource hash. The localization page separates literal RAW from formatter-based static reconstruction and reports the weapon-specific values without presenting reconstruction as an in-game screenshot. The concise map effect is consistent with the detailed eligibility explanation.",
      "The image receipt verifies icon ID 050/path separately from its attachment URL, matching hash, 128×128 dimensions and display verification. The config and extension draft agree on all config fields; the draft-only derived tier_table matches config.tiers. Required tuple/string/kind shapes pass.",
      "The parent-recorded focused link/GFM and generator checks pass; this focused peer review found no conflicting markup or unsynchronized reference."
    ],
